- id: llmvision_doorbell_ai
  alias: AI - Doorbell Motion Summary
  description: 'Reworked 2026-07-20: SDM motion events arrive 15-25s late, so live
    stream_analyzer frames showed the empty aftermath. Now waits 20s then analyzes
    the last ~60s of the doorbell RING BUFFER via video_analyzer, same pattern as
    the Airbnb side-door automation.'
  triggers:
  - trigger: state
    entity_id:
    - event.doorbell_motion
    - event.doorbell_chime
    - event.front_door_motion
    - event.front_door_ding
  conditions:
  - condition: template
    value_template: "{{ this.attributes.last_triggered is none or\n   (now() - this.attributes.last_triggered).total_seconds()
      > 120 }}"
  actions:
  - delay: '00:00:20'
  - action: shell_command.check_clip
    data:
      cam: doorbell
      seconds: 60
  - action: llmvision.video_analyzer
    data:
      provider: 01KXYBGAGRTST9351Y7WAW94P3
      video_file: /media/doorbell_check.mp4
      max_frames: 10
      use_memory: true
      message: 'CAMERA CONTEXT: This is the front door camera of a private Denver
        home. It looks straight down the home''s own front entrance walkway - a narrow
        concrete path between this house and the neighbor''s white modern building,
        with a wooden privacy fence and landscaping on the right, ending at the street
        sidewalk in the distance. A doormat sits at the bottom of the frame. This
        walkway is NOT an alley - always refer to it as the front door, front walkway,
        or sidewalk. People moving toward the camera are approaching the front door;
        people moving away are heading out to the street.


        These frames are from the last ~60 seconds of continuous footage from this
        camera, captured just after motion was detected. Your memory contains a labeled
        reference photo of this front door walkway in its normal empty state. Compare
        the frames with that reference and report only what is NEW or DIFFERENT.
        Ignore lighting and shadow differences alone. IMPORTANT: a package, box,
        envelope, or bag left on or near the doormat or walkway that is not in the
        reference counts as important activity even if no person is visible - report
        it, e.g. "Package left on the doormat".


        You are writing a phone notification about front door camera activity. Only
        the first few words are visible, so lead with the single most important fact.
        Reply with ONE short sentence (max 12 words). Never start with filler like
        "The image shows", "A sequence of", or "There is" - start directly with the
        subject and action, e.g. "Amazon driver leaving a package", "Two visitors
        ringing the doorbell", "Package left on the doormat". Focus on people, deliveries,
        and vehicles. If nothing is new versus the reference, reply exactly: No activity.'
      include_filename: false
      max_tokens: 60
      store_in_timeline: true
      expose_images: true
      generate_title: true
    response_variable: doorbell_ai
  - variables:
      doorbell_key_frame: '{{ (doorbell_ai.key_frame | default('''')).replace(''/media'',
        ''/media/local'') }}'
  - condition: template
    value_template: '{{ not (doorbell_ai.response_text | trim | lower).startswith(''no
      activity'') }}'
  - action: notify.mobile_app_brian_s_z_flip_7
    data:
      title: '{{ doorbell_ai.title | default(''Front Door'', true) }}'
      message: '{{ doorbell_ai.response_text }}'
      data:
        image: '{{ doorbell_key_frame }}'
        clickAction: /mobile-test/cameras
        url: /mobile-test/cameras
        tag: doorbell-ai
        group: cameras
        alert_once: true
        actions:
        - action: URI
          title: See Snapshot
          uri: '{{ doorbell_key_frame }}'
  - action: persistent_notification.create
    data:
      title: '{{ doorbell_ai.title | default(''Front Door'', true) }}'
      message: '{{ doorbell_ai.response_text }} ([view camera](/zenobia-home/camera-doorbell))'
  - if:
    - condition: template
      value_template: '{{ [''package'', ''deliver'', ''parcel'', ''courier'', ''amazon'',
        ''fedex'', ''usps'', ''dhl'', ''ups '', ''dropping off''] | select(''in'',
        ((doorbell_ai.title | default('''')) ~ '' '' ~ doorbell_ai.response_text ~
        '' '') | lower) | list | count > 0 }}'
    then:
    - action: notify.mobile_app_nick_iphone
      data:
        title: Package at the front door
        message: '{{ doorbell_ai.response_text }}'
        data:
          image: '{{ doorbell_key_frame }}'
          tag: doorbell-package
          group: cameras
  mode: single
  max_exceeded: silent
- id: llmvision_airbnb_door_tracking
  alias: AI - Airbnb Guest Door Tracking
  description: 'Reworked 2026-07-20 after a missed guest departure: SDM motion events
    arrive 15-25s late, so live-stream analysis saw empty frames. Now waits 20s then
    analyzes the last ~45s of the side_door RING BUFFER (the only source that reliably
    contains the person). Also triggers from Google Home person notifications via
    the phone relay, which often beat the SDM event.'
  triggers:
  - trigger: state
    entity_id: event.side_door_camera_motion
    id: sdm
  - trigger: state
    entity_id:
    - sensor.android_notification_phone_last_notification
    - sensor.brian_s_z_flip_7_last_notification
    attribute: post_time
    id: gh
  conditions:
  - condition: template
    value_template: '{{ trigger.id != ''gh'' or (trigger.to_state is not none and
      trigger.to_state.attributes.package == ''com.google.android.apps.chromecast.app''
      and ''side'' in ((trigger.to_state.attributes[''android.title''] | default(''''))
      ~ '' '' ~ (trigger.to_state.attributes[''android.text''] | default(''''))) |
      lower and ''person'' in ((trigger.to_state.attributes[''android.title''] | default(''''))
      ~ '' '' ~ (trigger.to_state.attributes[''android.text''] | default(''''))) |
      lower) }}'
  actions:
  - delay: '00:00:20'
  - action: shell_command.airbnb_ring_clip
    data: {}
  - action: llmvision.video_analyzer
    data:
      provider: 01KXYBGAGRTST9351Y7WAW94P3
      video_file: /media/airbnb_check.mp4
      max_frames: 10
      message: 'CAMERA CONTEXT: This camera watches the side entrance (the Airbnb
        guest door) of a private Denver home from above. The fenced side yard holds
        two air-conditioner units on gravel and a basement egress window; a concrete
        walkway runs along the bottom of the frame to the side door at the right edge.
        IMPORTANT: the walkway is a semi-public path - neighbors and passersby regularly
        walk along it without using the door. Refer to it as the side door or side
        walkway.


        This is the last ~45 seconds of continuous footage from the Airbnb guest
        entrance camera after motion was detected. Classify ENTERING or LEAVING ONLY
        if the person clearly interacts with the side door itself: the door opens
        or closes, they cross the threshold, unlock or knock on it, or stop directly
        at the door. A person merely walking through the frame along the walkway,
        in either direction, is a passerby - classify that as PASSING, never as ENTERING
        or LEAVING. Reply with exactly two lines: line 1 is one word only - ENTERING
        (person went in through the door), LEAVING (person came out of the door),
        PASSING (person visible but did not interact with the door), or UNCLEAR (no
        person visible, or you cannot tell). Line 2 is one short factual sentence
        describing what happened.'
      include_filename: false
      max_tokens: 80
      store_in_timeline: true
      expose_images: true
      generate_title: true
    response_variable: door_ai
  - variables:
      door_ai_key_frame: '{{ (door_ai.key_frame | default('''')).replace(''/media'',
        ''/media/local'') }}'
      door_ai_detail: '{% set lines = door_ai.response_text.split(''\n'') | map(''trim'')
        | reject(''eq'', '''') | list %} {{- (lines[1] if lines | length > 1 else
        '''') | trim }}'
  - choose:
    - conditions:
      - condition: template
        value_template: '{{ (door_ai.response_text | trim | upper).startswith(''ENTERING'')
          }}'
      sequence:
      - action: input_boolean.turn_on
        target:
          entity_id: input_boolean.airbnb_guest_downstairs
      - action: notify.mobile_app_brian_s_z_flip_7
        data:
          title: Airbnb - Guest arrived
          message: '{{ door_ai_detail if door_ai_detail else ''Guest entered through
            the side door.'' }}'
          data:
            image: '{{ door_ai_key_frame }}'
            clickAction: /airbnb-dashboard
            url: /airbnb-dashboard
            tag: airbnb-door
            group: cameras
      - action: persistent_notification.create
        data:
          title: Airbnb - Guest arrived
          message: '{{ door_ai_detail if door_ai_detail else ''Guest entered through
            the side door.'' }} ([view camera](/zenobia-home/camera-side-door))'
    - conditions:
      - condition: template
        value_template: '{{ (door_ai.response_text | trim | upper).startswith(''LEAVING'')
          }}'
      sequence:
      - action: input_boolean.turn_off
        target:
          entity_id: input_boolean.airbnb_guest_downstairs
      - action: notify.mobile_app_brian_s_z_flip_7
        data:
          title: Airbnb - Guest left
          message: '{{ door_ai_detail if door_ai_detail else ''Guest exited through
            the side door.'' }}'
          data:
            image: '{{ door_ai_key_frame }}'
            clickAction: /airbnb-dashboard
            url: /airbnb-dashboard
            tag: airbnb-door
            group: cameras
      - action: persistent_notification.create
        data:
          title: Airbnb - Guest left
          message: '{{ door_ai_detail if door_ai_detail else ''Guest exited through
            the side door.'' }} ([view camera](/zenobia-home/camera-side-door))'
  mode: single
  max_exceeded: silent
- id: camera_event_recording
